{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/5035","id":1599538234,"node_id":"PR_kwDOELj1_s5fVwQ6","html_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/5035","diff_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/5035.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/5035.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/issues/5035","number":5035,"state":"closed","locked":true,"title":"fix(client+server): avoid losing type information w/ index signatures","user":{"login":"jussisaurio","id":22619982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio","html_url":"https://github.com/jussisaurio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jussisaurio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #5034\r\n\r\n## 🎯 Changes\r\n\r\nWhen dealing with objects that have an index signature and known properties, such as:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  [x: string]: unknown;\r\n  foo: string\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you use `Omit`, `Pick` or `keyof` in any capacity, the resulting iteration loses type information because the key collapses to just `string | number` due to how union types work:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  type Foo = keyof { [x: string]: unknown, foo: string } // string | number. \r\n  \r\n  // string | 'foo' collapses to just ---> string\r\n  // number is included because objects can be accessed with number keys as well\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is intended behavior in TypeScript, see e.g. [this TS issue](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/45367) and linked related issues of the same issue.\r\n\r\nThis means to support use cases with such types, we need to carefully construct our key iterating functions to handle these edge cases, IF we want to support them at all. This PR changes the behavior of a few utility functions to use a new `WithoutIndexSignature` type-level function that handles this case. \r\n\r\nThe PR also adds a new regression test for the linked issue.\r\n\r\n## ✅ Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have followed the steps listed in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\r\n- [ ] If necessary, I have added documentation related to the changes made.\r\n- [x] I have added or updated the tests related to the changes made.\r\n","created_at":"2023-11-13T20:13:22Z","updated_at":"2023-12-16T00:05:49Z","closed_at":"2023-11-15T20:22:17Z","merged_at":"2023-11-15T20:22:17Z","merge_commit_sha":"6f968bd9e4000df7d8d20884c50fa9b07d8c490c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":2728304521,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzI4MzA0NTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/@trpc/server","name":"@trpc/server","color":"9BE78E","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3069276128,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDY5Mjc2MTI4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/labels/%E2%99%BB%EF%B8%8F%20autoupdate","name":"♻️ autoupdate","color":"64EE48","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/5035/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/5035/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trpc/trpc/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https: